# Diffusers lazy imports

New public classes must be listed in `_import_structure` (and the matching
`TYPE_CHECKING` import block) or `from diffusers import Foo` fails.

- Add the name to the submodule's list in the nearest `__init__.py` **and**
  `src/diffusers/__init__.py` when it is a top-level export.
- Don't import the class at module top-level in those files — the map is
  what makes the lazy module work.
- After adding a public object, CI's `utils/check_dummies.py` /
  `utils/check_inits.py` must still pass.

```python
# ❌ BAD — class file exists, map unchanged
# src/diffusers/schedulers/scheduling_foo.py  (new)
# src/diffusers/__init__.py                   (untouched)

# ✅ GOOD
_import_structure["schedulers"].append("FooScheduler")
```

See the comment at the top of `src/diffusers/__init__.py`.
